== 9. What this still cannot say ===============================
  1. Nothing here is a methylation-expression relationship. It is a
     comparison of methylation levels between groups of cell lines.
     The expression side remains at the floor in melanoma (0 of 39 lines
     with both measurements reached TPM >= 1).
  2. Cell lines are not tumours. The core-minus-distal statistic removes
     per-line global differences, which is the main culture objection, but
     it does not make a cultured line a melanoma in a patient.
  3. Lineage is an observational grouping. Melanoma lines differ from
     other lineages in many ways besides being melanoma.
  4. A melanoma-specific methylated-and-silent promoter is consistent
     with methylation-associated silencing. It does not establish that
     methylation CAUSED the silencing; that needs demethylation in vitro.
